{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>מטה משפט</b> (Perverting justice): one who knows the law and perverts it with his proofs. Or a fraudulent litigant — he misleads the blind."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads טוען שקד, literally 'a claimant of almond'; rendered here as 'fraudulent litigant' based on the idiom שקד/שקר, though the precise form is unusual."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:50.526741225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}